  "notes": "Discovery date backdated to July 17, 2023 (condition report initiation) per licensee's own determination that information sufficient to identify the out-of-tolerance condition existed at that time, even though the condition was actually recognized on August 29, 2023 during an extent-of-condition review triggered by an unrelated Notice of Violation (ML23201A132). Conversion factors had been out of tolerance since initial plant setup, so no discrete 'trigger' event exists in the narrative beyond the original configuration-control failure. Remaining TS 3.4.7 RCS leakage detection channels are stated as having remained operable, modeled as backup context in the consequence narrative but no explicit System node created since no specific instrumentation system name/EIIS code was given in narrative for the alternate channels."
